## Independent research

- [County-level study of Beacon and youth suicide rates](https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2025.04.22.25326214v2.full): Third-party research, not GoGuardian marketing material, and the strongest available external evidence for Beacon. Difference-in-differences and event-study analysis of 2018–2022 data comparing 70 counties with sustained Beacon implementation against 1,215 matched counties that never implemented it. Counties sustaining use had 24.4% lower youth suicide rates in 2021–2022 (p < 0.05). A sensitivity analysis defining implementation by initial adoption regardless of continued use found an attenuated association that was not statistically significant. Indexed in PubMed as PMID 41542696. Both findings should be cited together: the association is with sustained use, not with adoption alone.

